body:
Build the smallest plugin that answers one useful question. Start with Plugins → Add plugin → Code, select a Studio template, and run its preview before installing. A plugin adds a source, integration, notification channel, live TV source, extension, or whole content library.

## Choose a runtime
Hosted TypeScript runs inside QuickJS on wazero. There is no Node filesystem, process, environment, or direct networking. Use the permission-checked host services. Export `handle(request)` and return `{status, headers?, body}`. Calls on the hosted `ether` global are synchronous. SDK clients may be asynchronous in a sidecar; use `await` in portable SDK code.

Remote plugins run in your own process and serve HTTP or dial an outbound authenticated WebSocket tunnel. Their OS permissions are your responsibility. A remote plugin cannot use hosted folder grants or SecretGet; configuration is delivered through the remote configuration flow.

## First hosted handler
```ts
export function handle(req) {
  if (req.path === '/ether/health')
    return { status: 200, body: { status: 'ok' } };
  if (req.path === '/ether/test')
    return { status: 200, body: { ok: true, message: 'Ready' } };
  return { status: 404, body: { error: 'Unknown route' } };
}
```

Use [Manifest](/plugins/reference/manifest) to declare identity and runtime, [Capabilities](/plugins/reference/capabilities) to declare behavior, then [Testing](/plugins/reference/testing) before distributing a package. Expand the generated declarations on each page for exact signatures, limits, and validation errors. The Go validator is authoritative where optional wire fields have conditional requirements.

Declare `ether.settings` inline or as `{"$ref":"settings.schema.json"}`. Referenced files must be in the package. Public values come from `ether.settings.get()` per request; pooled hosted instances restart, so instance memory is not persistent configuration. Read secrets through SecretGet only in hosted code.

```json
{"fields":[{"key":"maxItems","kind":"number","label":"Maximum items"}]}
```

```ts
const maxItems = Number(ether.settings.get().maxItems ?? 12);
// POST /ether/configure validates proposed req.body:
return { status: 200, body: { errors: {} } };
```

Use `$t:key` labels with `ether.strings` and English fallback strings. Dynamic option fields should answer the SDK's options route. `contributes.setup.steps` groups settings fields and optional test routes. `/ether/v1/setup/{step}/test` receives `{step, fields}` and returns `{ok, detail, fields?}`; secrets stay out of that body. Required steps gate content-library sync and visibility until passed or owner-skipped. See the generated SetupStep and settings accessors for exact shapes.

Plugin-scoped string values survive instance restarts. Missing get returns null in JS; Go also returns a found flag. Use prefixes for list. Remote values are capped at 5 MiB, with the per-plugin quota also enforced. Never store secrets here.

```ts
ether.kv.put("counter", "1");
const value = ether.kv.get("counter");
```

The declarations and implementations below specify arguments, return types, defaults, permission checks, limits, and errors. SDK adapters translate raw hosted calls to portable clients. See [SDKs](/plugins/reference/sdk-typescript) and [Errors](/plugins/reference/troubleshooting).

Hosted fetch requires the destination in permissions.network. Redirect destinations are checked too. Read the generated MaxFetchBytes and transport limits; private or blocked destinations fail even if a hostname is declared. Handle upstream non-2xx status explicitly.

```ts
const r = ether.http.fetch({url: "https://api.example.org/status", method: "GET"});
if (r.status !== 200) throw new Error("Service unavailable");
```

The declarations and implementations below specify arguments, return types, defaults, permission checks, limits, and errors. SDK adapters translate raw hosted calls to portable clients. See [SDKs](/plugins/reference/sdk-typescript) and [Errors](/plugins/reference/troubleshooting).

Cache refs are content addressed blob:<sha256>, never filesystem paths. A library defaults to 2 GiB under a shared min(10 GiB, 5% of cache disk) cap; manifest and owner settings can override it. Remote blob uploads cap at 256 MiB. Use kinds for metadata and cache for bytes.

```ts
const ref = ether.cache.put("library-key", "cover.txt", "hello");
const data = ether.cache.open(ref);
```

The declarations and implementations below specify arguments, return types, defaults, permission checks, limits, and errors. SDK adapters translate raw hosted calls to portable clients. See [SDKs](/plugins/reference/sdk-typescript) and [Errors](/plugins/reference/troubleshooting).

Hosted only. Requires folders: read and a live owner-picked root. Paths are relative to the root. Traversal, symlink escapes and revoked grants fail. list/stat return metadata, never contents. hash returns size, Unix modTime, crc32, md5, sha1. Above 256 MiB use hashStart/hashPoll/hashCancel. Only requested files are hashed; unchanged files reuse the guarded digest cache. One active job per plugin, two process-wide; jobs yield while reading and abort if the file changes. See the full kinds guide for job lifecycle and revocation.

```ts
const job = ether.folders.hashStart("picked-root", "album.flac");
const status = ether.folders.hashPoll(job.id);
// Poll later until done, canceled, or error; never busy-loop.
// ether.folders.hashCancel(job.id);
```

The declarations and implementations below specify arguments, return types, defaults, permission checks, limits, and errors. SDK adapters translate raw hosted calls to portable clients. See [SDKs](/plugins/reference/sdk-typescript) and [Errors](/plugins/reference/troubleshooting).

Use structured SDK logs or hosted ether.log for bounded diagnostics. Host logs are redacted and rate limited, but do not send secrets in the first place. abort throws a classified aborted fault. Hot-path code has only log and abort.

```ts
ether.log("Refreshing one page");
// ether.abort("Missing required metadata");
```

